== Personality ==
Rover is a calm, kind figure. Despite being an amnestic, they show no complete dejection over their condition. If anything, Rover makes it clear that despite their search for their lost past, they also invoke the need to discover what the world has to offer them, including the journey they travel that brims with new novel sounds, stories, and the people they meet. As such, despite being stoic and expressionless at times, they are approachable and make friends with many of the playable characters who each take a liking to them. Having no problem whether they are human or not, only their nature.

While quiet, the Rover is willing to aid those in need, no matter the circumstances behind it. Even when told by [[Jinhsi]] that they did not have to join the battle against the [[Threnodian]], [[Ovathrax]], they support regardless and take part during the battle. Showing courage and bravery, putting the well-being of others despite not knowing them, while humbly working alongside the numerous characters they meet during their time in [[Jinzhou]]. As such, they are quick to become angered whenever one of their companions is caught in danger, such as [[Yangyang]] who had been sent away by [[Scar]]. They also place trust in others, even those who seemingly betray it as [[Yinlin]] did, can be regained, showcasing their ability in seeing the good people have. This in turn causes Rover to hold a dislike, at times disdain, towards those who treat human lives as tools. An example being Dollmaker that Rover showed no sympathy towards due to the criminal's action in disregarding those who he could have helped, but treated them without care. The same going towards the [[Tethys System]], whom Rover disliked over it's apathetic nature and decisions in both it's willingness to sacrifice individual humans and disregard towards the [[The Shorekeeper|Shorekeeper]] as a person.

This trait stems from their past-self, with flashbacks and information from the Shorekeeper revealing that they wished to unite humanity against the [[The Lament|Lament]] and the danger it possessed. Professing that no unique or even chosen group can stop it, and thus humans must come together as one. Taking nothing for granted, Rover enjoys what civilization offers, and believes that salvation comes from where nobody needs to be saved, thus why until that day, human lives gone shouldn't be treated in vain. Putting in their full effort to find a way to stop the Lament no matter how much time passes, or even where they travel to, even if it meant purposely losing their own memories.

However, they can also be rather ruthless at times. When they discover how Medulius, someone who took joy in bloodshed and desired for Aulus to be killed by his daughter, Verbia, Rover attempted to murder them in disgust. They were also suspicious and never truly trusted [[Phrolova]], wary and cautious of her the entire time. While they did hold some level of sympathy towards her when discovering her past, they believed her to be obsessed and when attempting to attain Leviathan's gem, they purposely threw their sword at her, killing her physical form. At the same time, Phrolova accuses them of discarding bonds with friends and allies, pointing out that they purposely wiped their own memory for a chance in solving the Lament, even if it meant breaking previously made promises, something the Rover doesn't deny. 

Although, while Rover is considerably heroic, some of their other traits include a weariness in doing certain requests that may stem from finding it bothersome. They also ask for compensation for such deeds, a quirk that the [[Ebony Gatekeeper]] says was rather normal for them. Likely from realizing some of their participation in certain activities, such as the [[Lollo Campaign]], may have complications when joining in.

== Backstory ==
There is have very little information about Rover, but due the relation with The Sentinel, Black Shores and the intro game video, they are at least one of two 'Instances' that had been sent to Solaris-3 (Event O), [[Resolution K626]] as Instance One. The another Instance is Instance Two, who is [[Shorekeeper]] based on the information about her: development base experience of Sonoro Theory and set under control of Tethys System.

Rover could be a term for Instance One in K626, because there might have been another Rover had been sent before, could be on same time with the Sentinel (need information).